{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01DyS41VWvGNRRbT5HUX4uxw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good! The profile text IS being generated. So the fallback code should be running. Let me check if it's hitting the condition. Oh wait, I see the issue - the fallback checks `if not appearance and not personality and not voice_guidance and profile`, but it's checking the variables AFTER they've been cleaned by `_clean_dict`. If the LLM IS returning the structured fields but they're all \"unknown\", they get cleaned to None, and then the fallback kicks in. But the fallback is using the `profile` variable which is the plain text, not the structured output.\n\nActually, looking at the code flow more carefully, I see that `char.description = profile` is being set, which adds to the `descriptions` array. So the profile text IS being saved. The issue is that the structured fields aren't being populated.\n\nLet me trace through the logic:\n1. LLM returns result with keys (profile, evidence, confidence, maybe appearance/personality/voice_guidance)\n2. We extract appearance/personality/voice_guidance\n3. We clean them with _clean_dict (which returns None if all values are \"unknown\")\n4. If all three are None AND profile exists, we try to structure the profile text\n5. But the structuring is using a second LLM call\n\nLet me check if the second LLM call is succeeding. Let me add better error handling:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":364,"cache_read_input_tokens":85574,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":364,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"929676b2-7950-46f1-85c2-2d385f38c640","uuid":"44002205-40b1-4178-9e3d-2be436cb4f0d"}
